From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:37:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let places check and repair the app's sealed databases

places_api gains sealed_database_check and sealed_database_repair,
sql-support's check and repair for any database an app seals through
obfsvfs, the logins' and autofill's as well as places' own, with the
Kotlin bindings regenerated from the megazord. A repair says how many
tables and rows it kept, how many pages it could not read, and how
many rows it dropped for referring to a row lost with them.

The stage 3 spike's patch 0012, and 0016's places, as one
(encri-firefox, W25).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
